  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "She first appears at Tian Ti Mountain when Hu Immortal Inheritance opens for the elite disciples of Central Continent’s ten great ancient sects. A Gu Immortal exchange names her as Spirit Affinity House’s outstanding junior and as someone’s granddaughter, and the crowd’s gaze settles on her as first place in that long competition. The text describes a phoenix coronet, slanted eyes, thin golden brows, a small red birthmark between the brows, and a bearing that makes the other elite disciples look ordinary beside her. Fang Zheng has already fought her and lost in six moves. When the Gu Immortals call the disciples in by ranking, she turns into golden light, becomes a phoenix, and enters the gatehouse first.",
      "chapters": [
        365
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_tian_ti",
        "inh_hu_immortal_inheritance",
        "fac_ten_great_ancient_sects",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_spirit_affinity_house",
        "char_fang_zheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She wears a phoenix coronet. She has slanted eyes, and her golden brows are thin and long. There is a small red birthmark in the middle of her brows. Her appearance is dignified and graceful, and her beauty is unrivalled. Her skin is like snow and her eyes are like lightning. She turns into a golden light that becomes a phoenix.",
      "chapters": [
        365
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal Crane Sect talk places her in the first tier of that generation with Ying Sheng Ji and Xiao Qi Xing: disciples with Gu Immortal backing, heavy resources from the start, and occasional Gu Immortal guidance. Lord Sky Crane tells Fang Zheng that Feng Jin Huang of Spirit Affinity House crushed the competition, and that Fang Zheng’s loss to her was normal.",
      "chapters": [
        366
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reputation-among-elite-disciples",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "char_ying_sheng_ji",
        "char_xiao_qi_xing",
        "char_lord_sky_crane"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang later names the same trio when he explains why Immortal Crane Sect needed a secret chess piece.",
      "chapters": [
        375
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reputation-among-elite-disciples",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_he_feng_yang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Dang Hun Mountain the lead group narrows to Xiao Qi Xing, Ying Sheng Ji, Feng Jin Huang, and Fang Zheng.",
      "chapters": [
        388
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reputation-among-elite-disciples",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_dang_hun_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "While still elsewhere, Fang Yuan already treats that inheritance as the foundation that made her a world-shaking Gu Immortal in his previous life.",
      "chapters": [
        365
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reputation-among-elite-disciples",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s prior-life recall of her biography lists three great opportunities: dream wings coming to her in sleep at age three, Hu Immortal blessed land on the day of that climb, and later fame that ends when he and demonic Gu Immortals kill her for Dang Hun Mountain. The same memory says dream wings would make the Hu Immortal climb hers.",
      "chapters": [
        399
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "second-great-opportunity",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "char_fairy_bai_hu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Near the peak she refuses to lose, calls dream wings, and grows a pair of Immortal Gu wings that let her overtake Fang Zheng even though she is still a mortal and the forced activation damages her soul. Watching Gu Immortals name the worm the legendary Immortal Gu Dream Wings. She reaches the cliff edge one step from victory, then Fixed Immortal Travel drops a naked Fang Yuan onto the peak ahead of her. He recognizes her from the Biography of Feng Jin Huang timing, kicks her off the mountain while she is too spent to resist, and takes Hu Immortal blessed land as its master.",
      "chapters": [
        405
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "second-great-opportunity",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this life the second opportunity fails.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "second-great-opportunity",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Back at Spirit Affinity House she sits by an ancient lake, unable to forget the kick to her face, then erupts and wrecks a valley with fire and punches while her parents watch. The text names Fairy Bai Qing as her biological mother and a rank six Gu Immortal, and Feng Jiu Ge as her father, then a rank seven Gu Immortal who once rose from the demonic path and was moved by Bai Qing into Spirit Affinity House. Bai Qing scolds him for drinking tea instead of worrying about their daughter, and he argues that the failure will help Feng Er mature because even they cannot protect her forever.",
      "chapters": [
        406
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "parents-and-the-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_bai_qing",
        "char_feng_jiu_ge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later restates that she has Gu Immortal parents and Spirit Affinity House support,",
      "chapters": [
        406
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "parents-and-the-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "and that her prior-life biography skipped earthly calamity worry for that reason.",
      "chapters": [
        408
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "parents-and-the-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After she returns home gloomy and trains to reclaim her pride, Feng Jiu Ge sends a letter arranging a battle between Fang Yuan and Feng Jin Huang, betting Spirit Affinity House’s glory against Immortal Crane Sect.",
      "chapters": [
        418
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "parents-and-the-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan refuses at first. A later recount notes that at the time of that challenge letter she had not yet reached rank five, which is why he treats the rank five letter sending green bird Gu as Feng Jiu Ge’s or Bai Qing’s rather than hers.",
      "chapters": [
        418
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "parents-and-the-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_letter_sending_green_bird_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "That is the earliest firm mortal-rank bound.",
      "chapters": [
        658
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "parents-and-the-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zhou Xiong Xin later labels her a rank five Gu Master during the fate war stretch.",
      "chapters": [
        1928
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "parents-and-the-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_zhou_xiong_xin",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She has phoenix eyes and a bright and beautiful face.",
      "chapters": [
        406
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "phoenix-eyes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a long sleep she wakes in a Spirit Affinity House building and tells Fairy Bai Qing that she has found dream wings’ true use: it can bring her into dream realms.",
      "chapters": [
        723
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She describes meeting life forms inside a dream and fleeing an old man who called himself Kong Jue; Bai Qing identifies him as Old Immortal Kong Jue, one of history’s three refinement path supreme grandmasters, and treats the trip as a real dream realm opportunity.",
      "chapters": [
        724
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_old_immortal_kong_jue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Reading The Legends of Ren Zu afterward, Feng Jin Huang says her refinement path realm has reached quasi-master level even though she had never practiced that path with interest, and she states that she walks on the metal path. She also still cannot read her father’s information path Immortal Gu because she is a mortal.",
      "chapters": [
        730
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan later agrees to meet her challenge through the Refinement Path Convention, narration says her defeat made her learn dream wings’ true use early, and that dream realm exploration has already pushed her refinement path attainment to quasi-grandmaster level with Fairy Bai Qing’s care.",
      "chapters": [
        847
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_refinement_path_convention"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the convention duel she wagers an immortal zombie revival method against a long-term guts Gu supply deal for Spirit Affinity House, because dream realm travel weakens her soul and guts Gu is among the best soul recovery methods.",
      "chapters": [
        852
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_guts_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The duel is a martial Gu refinement contest over five orifices fire pagoda Gu. She leads with refinement path killer moves, then Fang Yuan catches up on pure technique, interrupts her ink transformation killer move, and knocks her unconscious with backlash, after which the match ends in a draw for lack of materials on both sides.",
      "chapters": [
        856
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She chooses to trade wagers anyway, hands him the revival method, and later takes sixth place while the guts Gu trade with Spirit Affinity House moves ahead of Immortal Crane Sect in priority.",
      "chapters": [
        857
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In later Central Continent dream realm contests she still acts as Spirit Affinity House’s mortal representative with dream wings, Immortal Gu and immortal essence placed on her by Bai Qing, and no dream path mortal Gu recipes she is willing or able to sell.",
      "chapters": [
        911
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dream-realms-and-refinement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent",
        "sys_dream_path_mortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Zhao Lian Yun takes the Spirit Affinity House fairy seat and ascends ahead of her, Feng Jin Huang climbs alone, still mortal, still telling herself she must become a Gu Immortal for her parents. Duke Long of Heavenly Court stops a failed ice refinement, names her the future Great Dream Immortal Venerable, and says he has come to take her as disciple toward a rank nine throne because a dream path Immortal Gu chose her when she was young. The chapter title itself is “Great Dream Immortal Venerable Feng Jin Huang”.",
      "chapters": [
        1440
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "duke-long-and-great-dream",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_zhao_lian_yun",
        "char_duke_long",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_great_dream_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later recount of Fang Yuan’s previous life restates the same childhood dream wings sign and calls her the prospective Great Dream Immortal Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        2084
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "duke-long-and-great-dream",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spirit Affinity House then holds a grand master acknowledgement ceremony. Duke Long accepts her golden jade dew tea, calls her a refinement path great grandmaster, and names her his second disciple, with Red Lotus Demon Venerable as the unspoken first. He also tells Feng Jiu Ge that Feng Jin Huang is the prospective Great Dream Immortal Venerable and that Feng Jiu Ge is her Dao Guardian.",
      "chapters": [
        1442
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "duke-long-and-great-dream",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable",
        "sys_dao_guardian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under Duke Long she refines dream pillow Gu, a rank five dream path mortal Gu meant to let ordinary Gu Masters enter their own dream realms, and he keeps framing her successes as fate for the future Great Dream Immortal Venerable while she answers that she does not believe in fate.",
      "chapters": [
        1619
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "duke-long-and-great-dream",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_dream_pillow_gu",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Her accumulation is already enough for immortal ascension, but he stops her until she can advance her own body into the perfect Pure Dream Reality Seeker Physique she helped research through the shatter dream line.",
      "chapters": [
        1685
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "duke-long-and-great-dream",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_pure_dream_reality_seeker_physique"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Before the open battlefield stretch she sits opposite Fairy Zi Wei under Star Constellation Chessboard, pushing deduction until she passes out. Fairy Zi Wei notes that she is only a Gu Master, not a rank eight expert, and Duke Long then praises her for improving Pure Dream Reality Seeker Physique by using results from the killer move shatter dream.",
      "chapters": [
        1918
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "house_star_constellation_chessboard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the fate war Zhou Xiong Xin states that she is only a rank five Gu Master, yet can use the nine-nine consecutive unceasing formation to unleash shatter dream and turn dream realms into Pure Dream Reality Seeker Physique bodies.",
      "chapters": [
        1928
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Zi Wei recalls her through Central Heaven Gate so she can restrain Fang Yuan’s dream path methods from Immortal Gu House or formation cover, repeating the prior-life pattern in which her formation-backed dream path move spoiled his plan.",
      "chapters": [
        1946
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_central_heaven_gate",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "From that hidden Immortal Gu House she watches dreamy light smoke and cannot answer it with her own methods, while Spectral Soul and a controlled Fairy Zi Wei later mark her location and still refuse a quick seizure because her luck and Feng Jiu Ge’s protection make the attempt costly.",
      "chapters": [
        1948
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan closes on Heaven Overseeing Tower, Duke Long still treats her as the counter to Fang Yuan’s dream path methods, yet names her only a mortal Gu Master whose strength cannot match that Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        1960
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After fate Gu falls she weeps in a secret underground Immortal Gu House over the wasted sacrifice.",
      "chapters": [
        1961
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_fate_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the war Duke Long is dead, fate Gu is destroyed, and Feng Jiu Ge has betrayed Heavenly Court and gone missing. Heavenly Court debates whether to keep nurturing her: she was Duke Long’s disciple and the future Great Dream Immortal Venerable, but that certainty is gone, and Spirit Affinity House’s seed list slot is left empty while other sects still name candidates.",
      "chapters": [
        1970
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bai Qing later explains Feng Jiu Ge’s demonic immortal unification song to her as a sign that his feelings for their family had not ended when he left the righteous path.",
      "chapters": [
        1971
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan leaves Spectral Soul dream realms behind, Qin Ding Ling orders her to retrieve them.",
      "chapters": [
        2043
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_ding_ling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration again states that she is just a rank five Gu Master, not a rank six Gu Immortal, yet unique as Feng Jiu Ge’s daughter, and Heavenly Court immortals protect her while she collects the dream realms.",
      "chapters": [
        1928
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She remains a mortal dream path forerunner afterward. A Gu refinement trap arranged by rivals nearly kills her inside Spirit Affinity House; Zhao Lian Yun appears at the crisis, and later accounts say Zhao Lian Yun saved her even though the anti-Feng faction wanted her dead.",
      "chapters": [
        2088
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court still wants her kept and nurtured for dream path after fate Gu’s destruction, and leaves the collected dream realms with her.",
      "chapters": [
        2089
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She reaches dream path master attainment, keeps exploring dream realms for guts Gu and strength enough to protect Bai Qing, fulfill Duke Long’s dying wish to become a dream path Gu Immortal, and face Feng Jiu Ge on her own terms.",
      "chapters": [
        2091
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A later comparison still calls her just a mortal,",
      "chapters": [
        1440
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "while weighing dream path Immortal Gu recipes against Fang Yuan and Lady Poison Scorpion.",
      "chapters": [
        2097
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_recipe",
        "char_lady_poison_scorpion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Much later talk still treats Fairy Bai Qing’s daughter Feng Jin Huang as a living tie that keeps Bai Qing close to Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [
        2276
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-after",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
